IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgb1-s157-duties`

-- Tests for sgb1-s157-duties.l4 (Companies Act 1967, ss 157, 157A, 157B, 157C, 158, 159, 160; text lines 13170-13345 of CoA1967.txt).
-- Every expected value was written from the text of the Act, not from what the code printed; each group names the words it rests on.
-- JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.


-- s 157(5): "officer" includes a person who at any time has been an officer of the company; "agent" includes a banker, solicitor or auditor of the company and any person who at any time has been a banker, solicitor or auditor
#ASSERT `s 157(5) the person is an officer of the company for the purposes of section 157` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "includes": the list is open
#ASSERT `s 157(5) the person is an officer of the company for the purposes of section 157` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 157(5) the person is an agent of the company for the purposes of section 157` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "includes": the list is open
#ASSERT `s 157(5) the person is an agent of the company for the purposes of section 157` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 157(1): "A director must at all times act honestly and use reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office"
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the director has complied with the duty to act honestly and use reasonable diligence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not honest
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the director has complied with the duty to act honestly and use reasonable diligence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not diligent
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the director has complied with the duty to act honestly and use reasonable diligence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a director: the bearer named is the director
#ASSERT `s 157(1) the director has complied with the duty to act honestly and use reasonable diligence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 157(2): "An officer or agent of a company must not make improper use of his or her position ... or any information acquired by virtue of his or her position ... to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for himself or herself or for any other person or to cause detriment to the company"
-- improper use to gain an advantage
#ASSERT `s 157(2) the officer or agent contravenes the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- improper use to cause detriment to the company
#ASSERT `s 157(2) the officer or agent contravenes the subsection` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- improper use but neither purpose
#ASSERT `s 157(2) the officer or agent contravenes the subsection` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no improper use
#ASSERT `s 157(2) the officer or agent contravenes the subsection` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an officer or agent
#ASSERT `s 157(2) the officer or agent contravenes the subsection` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 157(3): "An officer or agent who commits a breach of any of the provisions of this section shall be -- (a) liable to the company for any profit made by him or her or for any damage suffered by the company as a result of the breach ...; and (b) guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"
-- a director who does not act honestly: breach of subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the officer or agent commits a breach of a provision of section 157` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a director who does not use reasonable diligence
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the officer or agent commits a breach of a provision of section 157` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- improper use to gain an advantage: breach of subsection (2)
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the officer or agent commits a breach of a provision of section 157` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a director who acts honestly and diligently and makes no improper use
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the officer or agent commits a breach of a provision of section 157` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither subsection is breached
#ASSERT `s 157(3) the officer or agent commits a breach of a provision of section 157` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- liable for any profit made
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(a) the profit for which the officer or agent is liable to the company` TRUE 500 EQUALS JUST 500
-- no breach: the subsection speaks of an officer or agent "who commits a breach"
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(a) the profit for which the officer or agent is liable to the company` FALSE 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- liable for any damage suffered
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(a) the damage for which the officer or agent is liable to the company` TRUE 700 EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(a) the damage for which the officer or agent is liable to the company` FALSE 700 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(b) the officer or agent is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no breach
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(b) the officer or agent is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an officer or agent
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(b) the officer or agent is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a fine not exceeding $20,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(b) the most the officer or agent may be penalised on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 157(3)(b) penalty` OF 20000, 12, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 157(3)(b) the most the officer or agent may be penalised on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 157(4): "This section is in addition to and not in derogation of any other written law or rule of law relating to the duty or liability of directors or officers of a company"
-- a flat negative
#ASSERT `s 157(4) section 157 derogates from the other written law or rule of law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- law not relating to the duty or liability of directors or officers: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 157(4) section 157 derogates from the other written law or rule of law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 157A(1): "The business of a company is to be managed by, or under the direction or supervision of, the directors"; (2): "The directors may exercise all the powers of a company except any power that this Act or the constitution of the company requires the company to exercise in general meeting"
-- managed by the directors
#ASSERT `s 157A(1) the business of the company is managed as the subsection provides` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- managed under the direction or supervision of the directors
#ASSERT `s 157A(1) the business of the company is managed as the subsection provides` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a bare "is to be" unmet: decided case by case (fork line in NOTES.md)
#ASSERT `s 157A(1) the business of the company is managed as the subsection provides` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a power no provision reserves to the general meeting
#ASSERT `s 157A(2) the directors may exercise the power of the company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "except any power that this Act ... requires the company to exercise in general meeting"
#ASSERT `s 157A(2) the directors may exercise the power of the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "except any power that ... the constitution of the company requires"
#ASSERT `s 157A(2) the directors may exercise the power of the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 157B: "Where a company only has one director, that director may make a declaration required or authorised to be made under this Act by recording the declaration and signing the record; and such recording and signing ... satisfies any requirement in this Act that the declaration be made at a meeting of the directors"
-- exactly one director
#ASSERT `s 157B the director may make the declaration by recording it and signing the record` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a "Where" gate on a "may" that fails: group 3, ruling (b)
#ASSERT `s 157B the director may make the declaration by recording it and signing the record` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no director: the "Where" gate fails
#ASSERT `s 157B the director may make the declaration by recording it and signing the record` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 157B the recording and signing of the declaration satisfies the requirement that the declaration be made at a meeting of the directors` 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- only "such recording and signing" is said to satisfy the requirement; the text is silent about any other way
#ASSERT `s 157B the recording and signing of the declaration satisfies the requirement that the declaration be made at a meeting of the directors` 1 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a "Where" gate that fails
#ASSERT `s 157B the recording and signing of the declaration satisfies the requirement that the declaration be made at a meeting of the directors` 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 157C(2): "Subsection (1) applies to a director only if the director -- (a) acts in good faith; (b) makes proper inquiry where the need for inquiry is indicated by the circumstances; and (c) has no knowledge that such reliance is unwarranted"
#ASSERT `s 157C(2) subsection (1) applies to the director` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "only if" (a) fails
#ASSERT `s 157C(2) subsection (1) applies to the director` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "only if" (b) fails
#ASSERT `s 157C(2) subsection (1) applies to the director` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "only if" (c) fails
#ASSERT `s 157C(2) subsection (1) applies to the director` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 157C(1): "Subject to subsection (2), a director of a company may, when exercising powers or performing duties as a director, rely on reports, statements, financial data and other information prepared or supplied, and on professional or expert advice given, by any of the following persons: (a) an employee ... whom the director believes on reasonable grounds to be reliable and competent ...; (b) a professional adviser or an expert in relation to matters which the director believes on reasonable grounds to be within the person's professional or expert competence; (c) any other director or any committee of directors upon which the director did not serve in relation to matters within that other director's or committee's designated authority"
-- (a) with the belief and subsection (2) met
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(a) an employee of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) without the belief on reasonable grounds: outside the words "whom the director believes"
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(a) an employee of the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) with the belief
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(b) a professional adviser or an expert` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) without the belief
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(b) a professional adviser or an expert` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c) matters within the designated authority
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(c) another director or a committee of directors on which the director did not serve` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) matters outside the designated authority
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(c) another director or a committee of directors on which the director did not serve` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a source not listed: the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1) a person not listed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not in good faith: subsection (2) "only if"
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(a) an employee of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no proper inquiry where indicated: subsection (2) "only if"
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(a) an employee of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- knowledge that the reliance is unwarranted: subsection (2) "only if"
#ASSERT `s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` `s 157C(1)(a) an employee of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 158(2) and (3): the persons to whom information may be disclosed, and the extent of the authorisation
#ASSERT `s 158(2) the information may be disclosed to the person` `s 158(2)(a) a person whose interests the director represents` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 158(2) the information may be disclosed to the person` `s 158(2)(b) a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the director may be required or is accustomed to act in relation to the director's powers and duties` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the text lists two persons without closing the list
#ASSERT `s 158(2) the information may be disclosed to the person` `s 158(2) another person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 158(3) the authorisation may be conferred in respect of the disclosure` `s 158(3)(a) all or any class of information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 158(3) the authorisation may be conferred in respect of the disclosure` `s 158(3)(b) only such information as may be specified in the authorisation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the text lists two extents without closing the list
#ASSERT `s 158(3) the authorisation may be conferred in respect of the disclosure` `s 158(3) another extent` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 158(1): "A director of a company may disclose information which the director has in his or her capacity as a director or an employee of a company, being information that would not otherwise be available to him or her, to the persons specified in subsection (2) if such disclosure is not likely to prejudice the company and is made with the authorisation of the board of directors"
#ASSERT `s 158(1) the director may disclose the information` TRUE `s 158(2)(a) a person whose interests the director represents` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 158(1) the director may disclose the information` TRUE `s 158(2)(b) a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the director may be required or is accustomed to act in relation to the director's powers and duties` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "if" gate on a "may": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 gives NOTHING (fork line in NOTES.md)
#ASSERT `s 158(1) the director may disclose the information` TRUE `s 158(2)(a) a person whose interests the director represents` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an "if" gate on a "may": no authorisation of the board
#ASSERT `s 158(1) the director may disclose the information` TRUE `s 158(2)(a) a person whose interests the director represents` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a person specified in subsection (2)
#ASSERT `s 158(1) the director may disclose the information` TRUE `s 158(2) another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not information of the kind described
#ASSERT `s 158(1) the director may disclose the information` FALSE `s 158(2)(a) a person whose interests the director represents` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 159: "The matters to which the directors of a company are entitled to have regard in exercising their powers include -- (a) the interests of the company's employees generally, as well as the interests of its members; and (b) the rulings of the Securities Industry Council ..."
#ASSERT `s 159 the directors are entitled to have regard to the matter in exercising their powers` `s 159(a) the interests of the company's employees generally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 159 the directors are entitled to have regard to the matter in exercising their powers` `s 159(a) the interests of the company's members` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 159 the directors are entitled to have regard to the matter in exercising their powers` `s 159(b) the rulings of the Securities Industry Council on the interpretation of the principles and rules of, and the practice to be followed under, the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "include": the list is open
#ASSERT `s 159 the directors are entitled to have regard to the matter in exercising their powers` `s 159 another matter` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 160(4): "This section does not apply to proposals ... made by a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking or property of the company appointed under a power contained in any instrument or a liquidator of a company appointed in a voluntary winding up"
#ASSERT `s 160(4) section 160 does not apply to the proposals` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(4) section 160 does not apply to the proposals` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- other makers: the text names two and says nothing of the rest
#ASSERT `s 160(4) section 160 does not apply to the proposals` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 160(1): "Despite anything in a company's constitution, the directors must not carry into effect any proposals for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property unless those proposals have been approved by the company in general meeting"
-- a disposal not approved in general meeting
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the directors are barred from carrying the proposals into effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless" met: approved by the company in general meeting
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the directors are barred from carrying the proposals into effect` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a disposal of the whole or substantially the whole: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the directors are barred from carrying the proposals into effect` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- subsection (4): proposals made by a receiver and manager
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the directors are barred from carrying the proposals into effect` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- subsection (4): proposals made by a liquidator in a voluntary winding up
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the directors are barred from carrying the proposals into effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 160(2): "The Court may, on the application of any member of the company, restrain the directors from entering into a transaction in contravention of subsection (1)"
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the Court may restrain the directors from entering into the transaction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a "may" gated by "on the application": group 3, ruling (b)
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the Court may restrain the directors from entering into the transaction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a transaction not in contravention of subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the Court may restrain the directors from entering into the transaction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 160(3): "A transaction entered into in contravention of subsection (1) is, in favour of any person dealing with the company for valuable consideration and without actual notice of the contravention, as valid as if that subsection had been complied with"
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the transaction is as valid as if subsection (1) had been complied with` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no valuable consideration: the text speaks only of a person dealing "for valuable consideration"
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the transaction is as valid as if subsection (1) had been complied with` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- actual notice of the contravention: the text speaks only of a person "without actual notice"
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the transaction is as valid as if subsection (1) had been complied with` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no contravention of subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the transaction is as valid as if subsection (1) had been complied with` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Regulative rules: each #TRACE has an EXPECT line above it naming the outcome the text gives. s 157(1) has "at all times" and no number of days, so it has no deadline a trace can miss: no breach path (NOTES.md).

-- the director acts honestly and diligently
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 157(1) a director must at all times act honestly and use reasonable diligence` "D" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 157(1) act honestly and use reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of the office of director` AT 3

-- nothing done: the obligation stays open, never BREACH
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 157(1) a director must at all times act honestly and use reasonable diligence` "D" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 157(2) an officer or agent must not make improper use of the position or of information` "O" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Officer "O" DOES `s 157(2) make improper use of the position or of information acquired by virtue of the position to gain an advantage or to cause detriment to the company` AT 8

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 157(2) an officer or agent must not make improper use of the position or of information` "O" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 160(1) the directors must not carry into effect proposals for disposing of the undertaking or property without the approval of the company` "D" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 160(1) carry into effect proposals for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property without the approval of the company in general meeting` AT 8

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 160(1) the directors must not carry into effect proposals for disposing of the undertaking or property without the approval of the company` "D" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8
